INSERT IGNORE INTO `npc_emotes` (`id`, `emoteid`, `event_`, `type`, `text`) VALUES
(2573, 1427, 1, 0, 'Oh Rujark, mother of might - Give us power to win this fight!'),
(2574, 1428, 2, 1, '''s corpse yelps in pain and collapses.'),
(2575, 1428, 1, 1, 'rushes towards you with its fangs bared.'),
(2576, 1429, 1, 1, 'bares its teeth and issues a thunderous roar.'),
(2577, 1429, 2, 1, '''s corpse roars a final time as blood begins to fill its throat.'),
(2578, 1430, 1, 1, 'churns the earth with its hooves and rushes forward.'),
(2579, 1430, 2, 1, '''s corpse squeals as it spins into the earth.'),
(2580, 1431, 1, 1, 'advances with an echo of its former grace.'),
(2581, 1431, 2, 1, '''s corpse crumbles to a dust that leaves no trace of its former grandeur.'),
(2582, 1432, 2, 1, '''s corpse collapses into a broken pile of harmless pebbles.'),
(2583, 1432, 1, 1, 'rumbles to life and crashes towards you.'),
(2584, 1433, 1, 0, 'Fool!  We cannot allow any to violate this place!'),
(2585, 1433, 2, 1, '''s corpse says, ''The Jeweled Guard will make short work of you!'),
(2586, 1434, 1, 1, 'trudges toward you, glittering menacingly.'),
(2587, 1435, 1, 1, 'chatters angrily and attacks!'),
(2588, 1436, 1, 1, 'roars to life from the earth.'),
(2589, 1437, 2, 1, '''s corpse says, ''Great chunks of sand and crystal crumble to the earth. With barely a whisper, the great summoning lies still and powerless.'),
(2590, 1438, 1, 0, 'The curse has gifted me with many abilities, come let me show you the way to the underworld.'),
(2591, 1438, 2, 1, '''s decayed corpse falls to the floor as the taint from the curse drains from her body to reveal her true visage'),
(2592, 1439, 1, 0, 'You come to destroy the master so I must destroy you instead.'),
(2593, 1439, 2, 1, '''s corpse falls to the ground no longer capable of moving on its own.'),
(2594, 1440, 1, 1, 'Lunges out with its spiked tendrils, focusing on its prey.'),
(2595, 1440, 2, 3, 'You hear the sound of something breaking open as the giant beast falls to the ground lifeless.'),
(2596, 1441, 1, 0, 'None shall defy the will of the keeper.'),
(2597, 1436, 2, 1, '''s corpse sinks back into the earth.'),
(2598, 1434, 2, 1, '''s corpse shatters into a myriad of shimmering fragments.'),
(2599, 1442, 1, 1, 'shakes off its paralysis and lunges at you.'),
(2600, 1442, 2, 1, '''s corpse stiffens as it becomes lifeless stone.'),
(2601, 1443, 1, 1, 'lumbers forward intent on crushing its victim.'),
(2602, 1443, 2, 1, '''s corpse disintegrates into a pile of stone.'),
(2603, 1444, 1, 1, 'coalesces from the shivering sands.'),
(2604, 1444, 2, 1, '''s corpse shudders as its features fade into a rush of sand.'),
(2605, 1435, 2, 1, '''s corpse shudders spasmodically in death.'),
(2606, 1445, 1, 1, 'whirls ahead in a squall of stinging sand.'),
(2607, 1445, 2, 1, '''s corpse flies apart with a spray of sand.'),
(2608, 1446, 1, 1, 'rises off its haunches with its claws outstretched.'),
(2609, 1447, 1, 0, '''Fools!  You will soon see the futility of your arrogance!'''),
(2610, 1446, 2, 1, '''s corpse shudders violently as it transforms into lifeless stone.'),
(2611, 1210, 1, 1, 'lumbers toward you with a singular purpose.'),
(2612, 1448, 4, 0, 'I want to get off the land and get me sea legs back!'),
(2613, 1449, 4, 0, 'Well, that was a job I won''t soon forget! Darned magnificent boat.  Chef Chowderly over on the Queen of Thorns was kind enough to send us all some nice pies for our hard work!'),
(2614, 1450, 4, 0, 'We finally found a way to make some sturdy anchors. They are holding the boat in place out in the Abysmal Sea quite nicely.'),
(2615, 1451, 4, 0, 'I decided to remain here in Nedaria''s Landing should the boat ever have to return or if we need to make another boat.  We already had to build the Thorn of the Tides, the wee boat that will carry folk from here to the Queen of Thorns.  Ya just never know when there''s gonna be more work.'),
(2616, 1452, 4, 0, 'I''ve spent many a year on the seas of Norrath, friend. As much as I''ve seen, I''ve never seen a ship greater than the Queen of Thorns.'),
(2617, 1453, 4, 1, 'gives you a slight nod and turns a wistful eye to the sea.'),
(2618, 1454, 4, 0, 'The crew shaped up nicely. I have faith that they will keep the Queen of Thorns in good stead.'),
(2619, 1455, 4, 0, 'Still some back-breakin'' work to be done here, friend. Best be keepin'' outta the way as we work. It''s dangerous.'),
(2620, 1456, 4, 0, 'Hail there, friend.  Have you had a chance to visit the Queen of Thorns?  I''ve been a couple of times.  Absolutely amazing.  The night before it left, the shore was filled with Wayfarers Brotherhood folk that signed on to man the boat.  What a night that was!  Lots of ale and dancing.  Someone named Jeffroy was utterly out of control with his ale and tripping over everyone!'),
(2621, 1457, 4, 1, 'whittles a piece of wood with a small, sharp knife.  It looks like it''s a miniature of the Queen of Thorns.'),
(2622, 1458, 4, 1, 'beams and bows to you. ''Yep, I sure was one of the folk that pieced that mighty boat together. Sorry to see it go!'),
(2623, 1459, 4, 0, 'Can ye smell that fresh sea air? Marvelous, ain''t it?'),
(2624, 1460, 1, 0, 'You dare challenge the champ? I will crush you like everyone else!'),
(2625, 1461, 1, 0, 'I will stretch your flayed skin over a drum and craft your bones into instruments of music!'),
(2626, 1461, 5, 0, 'Earless tone-deaf miscreant.  If you cannot differentiate pitch, perhaps you can know the difference between life and death.'),
(2627, 1462, 1, 3, 'The banshee opens her fetid mouth and a painful song assails your ears.'),
(2628, 1462, 2, 3, 'Black blood pools on the floor where the broken banshee lies.'),
(2629, 1463, 1, 1, 'opens its palm in sudden surprise.'),
(2630, 1463, 2, 1, '''s corpse says, ''Maestro, please forgive me...'),
(2631, 1464, 1, 0, 'You seek to challenge me within my own realm? You will know the true meaning of hate!'),
(2632, 1464, 5, 1, 'laughs. ''A pathetic display of feigned valor. May your god have pity on your weakness.'),
(2633, 1464, 2, 0, 'This is no victory, mortals! We shall meet again soon. Very soon...'),
(2634, 1465, 1, 3, 'I LIVE! Prepare yourselves, mortals. You will bow before the terrible might of the Prince of Hate!'),
(2635, 1465, 5, 1, 'laughs. ''A pathetic display of feigned valor. May your god have pity on your weakness.'),
(2636, 1466, 2, 1, '''s corpse says, ''My soul for you. Hatred will always be the path to true enlightenment!'),
(2637, 1466, 1, 0, 'I can no longer sit idly by, Innoruuk. These pathetic wretches will die by my hand as well.'),
(2638, 1465, 2, 1, '''s corpse shouts, ''No, it cannot end like this!'),
(2639, 1461, 2, 1, '''s corpse says, ''This dance is over, for now.'),
(2640, 1467, 2, 0, 'Careful which paths you follow in life, mortals! Fill yourself with hate and you will become a tool of Innoruuk.'),
(2641, 1467, 1, 1, 'shouts, ''All praise Innoruuk, our lord and creator!'),
(2642, 1468, 1, 1, 'raises its scepter and calls out, ''Finally, a chance to practice our tactics. Constructs, destroy their support troops!'),
(2643, 1469, 1, 1, 'rumbles to life.'),
(2644, 1470, 2, 0, 'How can this be? Beaten by such weaklings? Xocik! Kill Kreshin or you shall suffer my wrath from the other side.'),
(2645, 1471, 2, 3, 'Xocik writhes in pain as his body falls to the floor. Your valiant efforts have resulted in the rescue of Kreshin'),
(2646, 1472, 2, 3, 'The bone pile crumbles and alerts the nearby Muramites that rush to ambush you!'),
(2647, 1473, 1, 1, 'gnashes its wide jaws filled with deadly teeth and swims for its next meal'),
(2648, 1474, 1, 0, 'Come brothers and sisters.  Let us cleanse this place of the filth that has invaded our temple starting with these infidels!'),
(2649, 1475, 1, 2, 'I will kill you and your lickspittle friends for this!'),
(2650, 1475, 2, 0, '''s corpse says, ''Every man''s time comes.'''),
(2651, 1476, 2, 3, 'Swinging her weapon one last time, the massive entity falls to her side with a thud. While she was a creature consumed with destruction, her death is still graceful. As her bloodstained braids come to a rest on the floor and her muscles relax, you can''t help but wonder what could make such a magnificent creature so deadly.'),
(2652, 1477, 2, 3, 'The creature''s two heads face each other just before it falls to the floor, shaking the very foundation of the temple. Now there is nothing that stands between you and the being in charge of this invading army.'),
(2653, 1478, 8, 3, 'The King''s ice sphere explodes into a cloud of glittering shards.'),
(2654, 1479, 1, 1, 'flashes a sinister smile as the portals glow around him.'),
(2655, 1479, 5, 1, 'smiles as his opponent dies screaming'),
(2656, 1480, 8, 3, 'The Queen''s hurled flames explode upon impact.'),
(2657, 1481, 1, 1, 'begins whispering a sinister, arcane language.'),
(2658, 1482, 1, 1, 'levels her eyes at you and smiles viciously.'),
(2659, 1483, 1, 0, 'This will fill my time quite nicely. I was becoming bored.'),
(2660, 1484, 1, 1, 'smiles and flashes her claws as she prepares for battle.'),
(2661, 1485, 1, 1, 'smiles malignantly. ''You will make a lovely addition to my menagerie.'''),
(2662, 1486, 1, 0, 'Fool, you will be punished for this intrusion.'),
(2663, 1479, 2, 1, '''s corpse falls, as an earthquake loosens the foundation of Riftseeker''s Sanctum'),
(2664, 1487, 1, 1, 'rushes forward to protect its treasure.'),
(2665, 1487, 3, 1, 'cries out in failure, scrambling for the treasure as it crumbles to ash.'),
(2666, 1488, 1, 0, 'Get da weapons an'' smash em dead! Slay em all ''til da ground runs red!'),
(2667, 1488, 3, 1, 'falls as its face locks into a menacing smile.'),
(2668, 1489, 1, 0, 'Your bones will litter these gardens today!'),
(2669, 1489, 3, 3, 'The Kirin cries out, ''This cannot be!  I was destined to rule the temple!'''),
(2670, 1490, 1, 0, 'Out!  Out!  OUT!  You be makin'' a fine mess of me baths!  Get outta here before I make a nice meal o'' you!'),
(2671, 1490, 3, 3, 'Nethran walks three steps before collapsing upon himself in a small heap.'),
(2672, 1491, 1, 0, 'Rip, rip, rip em apart! Chew da guts and smash da heart!'),
(2673, 1491, 3, 1, 'collapses into a broken heap.'),
(2674, 1492, 1, 1, 'advances as its heavy metal feet leave cracks in the ground.'),
(2675, 1492, 3, 1, 'staggers and collapses into a pile of scrap metal.'),
(2676, 1493, 1, 1, 'growls and readies its weapons.'),
(2677, 1493, 3, 1, 'totters forward, flailing its bleeding limbs.'),
(2678, 1494, 1, 1, 'snarls and moves in to attack.'),
(2679, 1494, 6, 0, 'I gotz da kill! Look, look! Watch da blood spill!'),
(2680, 21476, 1, 1, 'swiftly moves to attack.'),
(2681, 21476, 2, 3, 'The essence of the spirit floats into the turbulent air.'),
(2682, 21477, 1, 1, 'strides forward to deal with its enemies.'),
(2683, 21477, 2, 1, '''s corpse staggers, then falls hard to the ground, whatever animating force it possessed now lost.'),
(2684, 12, 1, 1, 'strides forward to deal with its enemies.'),
(2685, 21478, 1, 1, 'gathers a greenish glow as it motions quickly with its hands. Then looks at you and says, ''Decay, corruption these me be!'''),
(2686, 21478, 3, 1, 'lets out one last breath as its life force slips away.'),
(21479, 21479, 1, 0, 'Time to die $name.'),
(21480, 21480, 9, 0, 'Let your death be a warning to all who dare oppose the Freeport Militia!'),
(21481, 21481, 7, 1, 'awakens from a deep slumber.'),
(21482, 21482, 3, 0, 'I underestimated your power... The Alto Roburon will be prepared next time!'),
(21483, 21483, 7, 0, 'Young one, you cannot fathom how long it has been since I breathed air and felt flesh on my bones. I told you I would show you a weapon that would make you the most powerful of your kind. I said nothing of giving it to you. Feast your eyes on Innoruuk''s Curse, mortal! Thank you for your service.'),
(21484, 21484, 1, 1, 'raises his axe over his head as the fire of war slithers across the blades.'),
(21485, 21484, 5, 0, 'You fool! Did you really think you could challenge the God of War?');
